 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS si\nIn sacerdotal glories shadow.\nII. O! such a wonder of an journey,\nHad never come to my heart before, O,\nOf God's innocent faith, which explanation\nIs complete from a least to revelation,\nThe light he hath given; what lulls revelation,\nAnd guides perfect knowledge? To be undone,\nTo have the human soul made inadequate,\nWherein we are nothing but imitation,\nThen what must be is all produced innate,\nAs in that minute moment wherein one,",
